Description: per-application volume mixer for PipeWire and PulseAudio [Trinity]
 tde-mixer is a volume mixer for the Trinity Desktop Environment that
 controls the sound server instead of the sound card, like the mixers of
 other current desktops. It replaces KMix in the system tray.
 .
 It shows a volume slider, mute button and level meter for each application
 that plays or records sound and can move an application to another output
 or input device. It sets the volume, port and default of each device and
 the profile of each sound card.
 .
 It is available as a standalone application, as a Trinity Control Center
 module (Sound & Multimedia > Volume Mixer), in System Settings, and as a
 system tray icon that handles the keyboard's volume keys and starts at
 login. It can turn off KMix's tray icon, but does not need KMix removed.
 .
 It talks to PipeWire natively or uses the PulseAudio protocol, which works
 with PulseAudio and with PipeWire's pulse server.
